@host = http://localhost:5187

# Story 47 - the customer portal: registration, sign-in, account, categories, tickets (submit, list, thread, reply, close,
# reopen) and the agent-side password provisioning. Run top to bottom against a Development API (`docker compose up -d`, then
# `dotnet run --project backend/src/Crm.Api --launch-profile http`).
#
# Story 59 seeds four more portal accounts (Mona, Yousef, Huda - revoked, Faisal - no requests): see demo-accounts.http.
# Seeded portal account: Ahmed (ahmed@example.com, Crm_Dev_2026!) - the primary contact of Ahmed Al-Qahtani (RYD-CARE, ticket
# T-000001), so he is the account admin of his customer. Access tokens live 2 minutes in Development: re-run the login blocks
# when a request answers 401. Portal register/login/refresh share ONE limit of 10 per minute per IP (RateLimiting:PortalSignIn);
# when a block answers 429, wait a minute. Counts in the expected results (T-000001 only, three categories) assume a fresh
# database; earlier story runs add tickets and categories.
#
# LEAK CHECK: search every portal response body for SECRET-NOTE-47, assignedAgent, departmentId, branchId, rowVersion,
# activities and priority - none may appear (request 10 plants the note).
#
# Dev seed: Najd Logistics (11000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002, RYD-CARE, ticket T-000002), Red Sea Trading
# (11000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003, JED-CARE, ticket T-000003, contact Fahad - portal access off).

@ahmedTicket = 15000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@najdTicket = 15000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@najd = 11000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@redSea = 11000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003
@fahad = 11000000-0000-0000-0001-000000000004
@general = 15000000-0000-0000-0001-000000000001
@internal = 15000000-0000-0000-0001-000000000004
@unknown = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000dead

### 1. Portal login as Ahmed - 200; Set-Cookie crm_portal_refresh=...; path=/api/Portal/Auth. Decode the token: aud crm-portal,
### customer_id, contact_id, portal_admin "true", portal_branch, portal_department, NO membership and NO role claims.
# @name portal
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ahmed@example.com", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

@portalToken = {{portal.response.body.accessToken}}
@portalRefresh = {{portal.response.body.refreshToken}}

### 1b. Wrong password - 401 Identity.InvalidCredentials (generic; the same for an unknown email)
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ahmed@example.com", "password": "not-the-password-1" }

### 2. Me - 200 isAccountAdmin true, permissions ["portal.account","portal.tickets"]
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Me
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 2b. Me without a token - 401
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Me

### 3a. A PORTAL token on the staff Me - 403 urn:crm:problem:forbidden (authenticated, wrong audience)
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Me
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 3b. A portal token on the agent inbox - 403
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 3c. A portal token on the admin users - 403
GET {{host}}/api/Admin/Users
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 3d. A portal token on the customer list and on the agent provisioning endpoint - 403
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 4. Staff login as agent A
# @name agentA
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "agent.a@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

@agentAToken = {{agentA.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4a. A STAFF token on the portal Me - 403
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Me
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 4b. A staff token on the portal tickets - 403
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 4c. Administrator (holds no portal permission) on the portal tickets - 403
# @name admin
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

###
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{admin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 4d. The PORTAL refresh token on the STAFF refresh endpoint - 401 (unknown there)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{portalRefresh}}" }

### 5. Categories - 200: the active, customer-visible categories of RYD-CARE (General, Technical, Complaint on a fresh database;
### never the Internal or Legacy ones, never RYD-BILL or JED-CARE categories)
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/TicketCategories
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 6. My tickets - 200: T-000001 (Received) and every other ticket of the customer (Ahmed is the account admin), newest activity first
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 6b. The closed tab - 200
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets?tab=closed
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 6c. Search by number - 200: T-000001 only
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets?search=T-000001
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 6d. Unknown status - 400 urn:crm:problem:validation
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets?status=Nope
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 6e. One portal status inside the tab - 200 (Received = New)
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets?status=Received&pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 7a. Another customer's ticket (Najd, T-000002) - 404 Tickets.TicketNotFound (never 403: it must not confirm the ticket exists)
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{najdTicket}}
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 7b. ... its thread - 404
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{najdTicket}}/thread
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 7c. ... a reply - 404
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{najdTicket}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

{ "body": "hello" }

### 7d. ... request closure - 404
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{najdTicket}}/request-closure
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 7e. ... reopen - 404
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{najdTicket}}/reopen
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 7f. An unknown id - 404 with exactly the same body shape as 7a
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{unknown}}
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 8. Raise a request in Arabic - 200: status Received, actions ["Reply","RequestClosure"], category General
# @name submitted
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

{
  "subject": "لا أستطيع تتبع شحنتي",
  "description": "رقم الشحنة لا يظهر في التطبيق.",
  "categoryId": "{{general}}"
}

@submittedId = {{submitted.response.body.id}}

### 8b. A category the customer may not pick (Internal) - 404 Tickets.CategoryNotFound
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

{ "subject": "x", "description": "y", "categoryId": "{{internal}}" }

### 8c. Empty subject - 400 urn:crm:problem:validation
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

{ "subject": "", "description": "y" }

### 9. Agent A sees it in the inbox - 200: channel Portal, department RYD-CARE, customer Ahmed, status New
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets?queue=all&pageSize=3
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 10. Agent A: an internal note (the leak bait) and a public reply - both 200
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{submittedId}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "SECRET-NOTE-47 do not show the customer" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{submittedId}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "مرحباً أحمد، نعمل على ذلك." }

### 11. The portal thread - 200: the agent reply only (sender "Support", no staff id or name), NO SECRET-NOTE-47, no activity
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{submittedId}}/thread
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 11b. The portal ticket - 200: no note text, assignee, department, rowVersion or activity anywhere
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{submittedId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 12. A customer reply - 200; then the agent's thread shows the inbound message (authorId and recordedById = Ahmed's contact id)
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{submittedId}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

{ "body": "شكراً، بانتظاركم." }

###
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{submittedId}}/thread
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 13. My issue is solved - 200: status Resolved, actions ["Reply","Reopen"]
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{submittedId}}/request-closure
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 13b. Reopen a Resolved ticket - 200: status InProgress
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{submittedId}}/reopen
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 13c. Request closure again - 200: Resolved
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{submittedId}}/request-closure
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 13d. Agent A reads the ticket, then closes it with the rowVersion of that response - 200
# @name agentTicket
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{submittedId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Tickets/{{submittedId}}/transitions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "action": "Close", "rowVersion": "{{agentTicket.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 13e. The customer reopens a CLOSED ticket - 422 Tickets.TransitionNotAllowed
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{submittedId}}/reopen
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

### 13f. A reply to a closed ticket - 422
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{submittedId}}/replies
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{portalToken}}

{ "body": "one more thing" }

### 14a. Registration - an unknown email - 204 (identical to every refusal; nothing is created)
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nobody@example.com", "password": "Portal_Pass_2026" }

### 14b. Ahmed's email again (already registered) - 204, nothing changes
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ahmed@example.com", "password": "Another_Pass_2026" }

### 14c. ... so login with that password - 401 (the original password still works)
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ahmed@example.com", "password": "Another_Pass_2026" }

### 14d. Fahad (portal access off) registers - 204; then login - 401
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "fahad@redsea.example.com", "password": "Portal_Pass_2026" }

### 14e. A malformed email / weak password - 400
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "not-an-email", "password": "short" }

### 15. Agent B (JED-CARE) enables portal access on Fahad: read the customer for its rowVersion, then PUT the contact - 200
# @name agentB
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "agent.b@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

###
# @name redSeaCustomer
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{redSea}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentB.response.body.accessToken}}

###
PUT {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{redSea}}/contacts/{{fahad}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentB.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "name": "Fahad", "email": "fahad@redsea.example.com", "hasPortalAccess": true, "rowVersion": "{{redSeaCustomer.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 15b. Fahad registers - 204; 15c logs in - 200 (his own password); 15d lists - T-000003 only; 15e asks for Ahmed's ticket - 404
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "fahad@redsea.example.com", "password": "Portal_Pass_2026" }

###
# @name fahadLogin
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "fahad@redsea.example.com", "password": "Portal_Pass_2026" }

###
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{fahadLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{ahmedTicket}}
Authorization: Bearer {{fahadLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### 16. Agent provisioning: agent A for Red Sea (JED-CARE, out of scope) - 403
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/PortalAccounts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "customerId": "{{redSea}}", "contactId": "{{fahad}}", "password": "Layla_Portal_2026" }

### 16a. Agent A adds Layla (portal access on) to Najd, then sets her password - 200 (creates the account)
# @name najdCustomer
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{najd}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

###
# @name layla
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{najd}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "name": "Layla Hassan", "email": "layla@najd.example.com", "isPrimary": false, "hasPortalAccess": true, "rowVersion": "{{najdCustomer.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

@laylaId = {{layla.response.body.contacts[2].id}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/PortalAccounts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "customerId": "{{najd}}", "contactId": "{{laylaId}}", "password": "Layla_Portal_2026" }

### 16b. An unknown contact - 404 Identity.PortalContactNotFound (a real contact whose portal access is off answers 422
### Identity.PortalAccessNotEnabled)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/PortalAccounts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "customerId": "{{najd}}", "contactId": "{{unknown}}", "password": "Layla_Portal_2026" }

### 16c. A weak password - 400
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/PortalAccounts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "customerId": "{{najd}}", "contactId": "{{laylaId}}", "password": "short" }

### 17. Layla (not the primary contact, so not the account admin) - login 200 with portal_admin "false"; her list is empty
### (T-000002 belongs to another Najd contact) and T-000002 is 404 for her
# @name laylaLogin
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "layla@najd.example.com", "password": "Layla_Portal_2026" }

###
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{laylaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###
GET {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets/{{najdTicket}}
Authorization: Bearer {{laylaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

###
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{laylaLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "subject": "Layla's request", "description": "Raised by a non-admin contact." }

### 19. Refresh: a new pair - 200; the OLD refresh token again - 401 and the whole session is revoked
# @name refreshed
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{portalRefresh}}" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{portalRefresh}}" }

### 20. Profile: rename and switch language - 200 (log in again first if the token expired)
PUT {{host}}/api/Portal/Me
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{refreshed.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "displayName": "Ahmed Q.", "preferredLocale": "en" }

### 20b. Change password: a wrong current password - 400 on CurrentPassword; the right one - 204 (run it, then log in with the new one)
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Me/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{refreshed.response.body.accessToken}}

{ "currentPassword": "wrong-wrong-1", "newPassword": "Brand_New_Pass_2026" }

### 21. Revocation: agent A turns Layla's portal access off - her refresh and login answer 401 (until it is turned back on)
# @name najdCustomer2
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{najd}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

###
PUT {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{najd}}/contacts/{{laylaId}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "name": "Layla Hassan", "email": "layla@najd.example.com", "hasPortalAccess": false, "rowVersion": "{{najdCustomer2.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{laylaLogin.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### 22. Logout - 204 and the cookie is cleared; the refresh token then answers 401
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{refreshed.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### 30. Rate limit: run this block 11 times inside a minute - the 11th is 429 with Retry-After and urn:crm:problem:rate-limited
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "nobody-rl@example.com", "password": "wrong-password-1" }

### 31. Register has the same limit (shared per IP) - after a minute, run it 11 times - the 11th is 429
POST {{host}}/api/Portal/Auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "rl@example.com", "password": "Portal_Pass_2026" }

### 32. Lockout: five wrong passwords lock the account for the lockout window (2 minutes in Development); the right password is
### then still 401 until the window ends or an agent resets the password (request 16a). Use a provisioned contact, not Ahmed.
